+## Fix round 1
+
+Review `task-6-review.md`, on top of `6dc1c956c`.
+
+### I1: writes to `.ROUTINES` refuse (controller ruling)
+
+`Loud::package_routines_write` (`lib.rs`, owner `Owner::Phase9`, text "a write to a package's
+.ROUTINES table is not implemented (Phase 9)") is raised by `hash.rs`'s `refuse_routines_write`
+when the receiver is a package's `.ROUTINES` table (`Interp::is_package_routines_table`, a scan of
+`package_tables`). It guards every store mutator a program or extension reaches: `store_put`
+(`put`, `[]=`), `store_entry_write` (`~name=`), `native_hash_remove`, `native_hash_remove_item`,
+`native_hash_empty`, `native_hash_set_entry`, `native_hash_remove_entry`, the `Directory`
+`setMethod`/`unsetMethod` pair, and the native API's `native_put` and `store_remove`. `~putAll`
+reaches `put` and refuses; `~putAll` of an empty collection writes nothing and answers.
+`~addRoutine` and the table's own build write through `directory_put` and are not guarded.
+
+Witness: `dispatch/tests.rs` `a_write_to_a_packages_routines_table_refuses`. Each of `put`, `[]=`,
+`~foo =`, `remove`, `removeItem`, `empty`, `setEntry`, `removeEntry`, `putAll` before `call foo`
+gives rc 120 with the refusal and no stdout; the reviewer's shape (`.routines~put(.routines~bar,
+'FOO')`) is the first. Adjacent success, also run on the oracle with identical output
+(`2 1`, `3`, `5`, `foo`, rc 0): `.routines~items`/`hasIndex`, `~addRoutine` then `items`, a
+`.methods['X'] = 5` write read back, and `call foo`.
+
+`refusal-sites.tsv` re-derived (`REXX_REFUSAL_SITES_REFRESH=1`): one new row,
+`package_routines_write`, filled in as `recorded`/`yes` with its witness; the other changed rows
+are `lib.rs` line shifts.
+
+### `.METHODS` and `.RESOURCES` writes stay allowed
+
+Oracle probe `/tmp/claude-1000/p9/t6-fx1/a.rex`: `.methods~put`, `~remove`, `[]=`, `~empty`,
+`.resources~put`, `~remove`, `~empty`, each followed by `Package~definedMethods`,
+`Package~resources` and `Package~resource(name)`, then `.routines~remove` followed by
+`Package~routines` and `~findRoutine`. Oracle stdout:
+`1 3`, `0 2`, `return 42`, `2 1`, `The NIL object 1`, `0 0`, `0 0`, `r1`, `0 The Object class`.
+At `6dc1c956c` the crate answers the same except the last line (`1 The Routine class`), which is the
+`.ROUTINES` divergence I1 refuses. In the oracle's source the only runtime readers of
+`unattachedMethods` are `getMethods` (`.METHODS`) and `getDefinedMethods`
+(`PackageClass.hpp:151,173`), and of `resources` `getResources` and the two resource readers
+(`PackageClass.cpp:1697,1720`). Each reads the same table, and the crate reads the same store for
+each. So a write changes nothing beyond what reads of the table answer, and the crate's reads agree.
+That is the reading of the ruling applied here. If the ruling meant the `Package` readers
+themselves as "behaviour beyond the table", the same guard extends to these two tables in one line.
+
